  "guards": [
    "Do not apply the 3-hour deadline to every KII incident; it is limited to an incident in a significant KII object.",
    "A computer attack notification under clause 3 has a 24-hour deadline even when a significant KII object is involved.",
    "For a financial-sector KII object, the Bank of Russia route under clause 4 is additional to, not a replacement for, the NCCCI route.",
    "The 90-calendar-day period starts on register inclusion and is not an incident-notification period.",
    "The 7-calendar-day period starts on plan approval and concerns sending the approved plan copy.",
    "The FSB Center's 30-calendar-day review rule in clause 8 is conditioned on inclusion of clause 7 provisions.",
    "For a financial-sector draft containing clause 7 provisions, clause 8 actions precede submission to the Bank of Russia.",
    "The 48-hour clause 14 deadline is a post-completion result report, not the initial attack or incident notice.",
    "Clause 16 contains an obligation to send information but no explicit numerical deadline; none may be invented.",
    "Hour deadlines are elapsed-hour maxima; only periods expressly stated as calendar days are encoded as CALENDAR_DAY."
  ]
